# Local Flutter SDK toolchain clone. On this machine `flutter` on PATH resolves
# to `./flutter/bin/flutter.bat`, i.e. a full SDK checkout (bin/, packages/,
# dev/, engine tooling, ~18k files) living inside the repository root. It is a
# vendored dependency of the environment, NEVER application source, so it must
# never be staged: without this rule a bare `git add -A` would push the whole
# SDK. Root-anchored on purpose so an unrelated nested folder is unaffected.
/flutter/

# Flutter / DevTools stray logs
*.log
# =========================
# =========================
# SECURITY NOTE (Qodo): ignore every environment-file variant — `.env`,
# `.env.production`, `.env.local`, `.env.staging`, `*.env`, etc. — so API keys,
# `.env.example` stays tracked as the template for local setup.
# Keep the canonical template committed — do NOT remove the line above:
# `!.env.example` re-includes the template that `.env*` would otherwise
# blanket-ignore.

# ==== ENV SECRETS (never commit) ====
# CI/pre-commit: run gitleaks (or equivalent secret scan) before pushing.
.env
.env.*
*.env.local
!.env.example
# Widget Preview related
.widget_preview/
